      "text": "The error comes from computing `2 ** k`. In the Qiskit version this question targets, `Parameter`/`ParameterExpression` has no `__rpow__`, so Python can't evaluate an integer raised to a `Parameter`. (Newer Qiskit versions may support this; I haven't checked that here.)\n\nThe fix rewrites `2**k` as `exp(k * ln 2)`. `ParameterExpression` supports multiplication by a float and has an `.exp()` method, and dividing a float by a `ParameterExpression` also works. So `theta` stays the same value, `2*pi/2**k`, as a symbolic expression.\n\n```python\nimport numpy\nfrom math import pi\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, QuantumRegister\nfrom qiskit.circuit import Parameter\n\nk = Parameter('k')\n\nq = QuantumRegister(2)\nCROT_circ = QuantumCircuit(q, name='CROT')\n\n# FIX: 2 ** k raises TypeError (int ** Parameter unsupported) -> rewrite 2**k as exp(k*ln2), because ParameterExpression supports multiplication and .exp()\ntheta = 2 * pi / (k * numpy.log(2)).exp()\nCROT_circ.cp(theta, 0, 1)\n\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
